      "content": "HIGH STREET 1 5252                                                   (East Side)                                                   Nos 65 to 69 (odd) TL 0507 1/12             18.6.48. II                       GV 2. Early C18.  Rainwater head dated 1714 with initials IW.  Purple brick, No 69 cement rendered and colour washed, Nos 65 and 67 dressed with red brick  Hipped tiled roofs with moulded wooden cornice, modillioned to No 65.  3 storeys, slightly recessed centre with pair of carriageways.  5:2:4 sash windows to upper floors. Early C19 shop window to No 65; modern shops to Nos 67 and 69 with C19 cornices. Nos 57 and 83 (odd) and No 63A and 79A form a group. Listing NGR: TL0554707880"
    }
